  "worked_solution": "First, note that the given equation is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(6x+{12}^{\u2218})=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n6x+{12}^{\u2218}={60}^{\u2218}+{360}^{\u2218}\\cdot n,\\,6x+{12}^{\u2218}={120}^{\u2218}+{360}^{\u2218}\\cdot n.\n$$\n\nSolving the two equations above for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6x & ={60}^{\u2218}-{12}^{\u2218}+{360}^{\u2218}\\cdot n, & \\,6x & ={120}^{\u2218}-{12}^{\u2218}+{360}^{\u2218}\\cdot n \\\\ 6x & ={48}^{\u2218}+{360}^{\u2218}\\cdot n, & \\,6x & ={108}^{\u2218}+{360}^{\u2218}\\cdot n \\\\ x & ={8}^{\u2218}+{60}^{\u2218}\\cdot n, & \\,x & ={18}^{\u2218}+{60}^{\u2218}\\cdot n.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have that $a={18}^{\u2218}.$",
